# ensure_anim_bp_event_graph_locomotion_driver Design

## Purpose

`ensure_anim_state_machine_sample_variant` can create sample states,
transitions, rule variables, and BlendSpacePlayer input bindings, but it does
not populate those variables at runtime. Automatic locomotion authoring needs a
bounded EventGraph route that updates variables such as `Speed`, `Direction`,
`IsInAir`, `Acceleration`, and `IsAccelerating` every animation tick without
requiring hand-authored Blueprint graph glue.

`ensure_anim_bp_event_graph_locomotion_driver` fills that gap for sample/temp
Animation Blueprints.

## Scope

- Source AnimBP is read-only.
- Target AnimBP must be under `/Game/_MCP_Sample` or `/Game/_MCP_Temp`.
- Target is duplicated or reused, never the original source.
- Finished content uses standard engine Blueprint nodes only:
  `Event Blueprint Update Animation`, `TryGetPawnOwner`, optional `IsValid`
  branch, `GetVelocity`, `VSizeXY`, `Set <SpeedVariable>`, optional
  `GetActorRotation`, `CalculateDirection`, `Set <DirectionVariable>`,
  `GetMovementComponent`, `IsFalling`, `Set <IsInAirVariable>`, optional
  `Cast To CharacterMovementComponent`, `GetCurrentAcceleration`,
  `Set <AccelerationVariable>`, float `>` compare, and
  `Set <IsAcceleratingVariable>`.
- No `/Script/UnrealMCP`, `/UnrealMCP`, `UnrealMCP`, `MCPUnreal`, or
  `mcp_unreal` references are persisted into generated assets.

## Authored Graph

Default graph shape:

```text
Event Blueprint Update Animation
  -> TryGetPawnOwner
  -> Branch(IsValid(PawnOwner))
  -> Set Speed(VSizeXY(GetVelocity(PawnOwner)))
```

Optional Direction shape:

```text
Set Speed
  -> Set Direction(CalculateDirection(GetVelocity(PawnOwner), GetActorRotation(PawnOwner)))
```

Optional IsInAir shape:

```text
Set Direction or Set Speed
  -> Set IsInAir(IsFalling(GetMovementComponent(PawnOwner)))
```

Optional Acceleration shape:

```text
Set IsInAir, Set Direction, or Set Speed
  -> Cast To CharacterMovementComponent(GetMovementComponent(PawnOwner))
  -> Set Acceleration(VSizeXY(GetCurrentAcceleration(CharacterMovement)))
```

Optional IsAccelerating shape:

```text
Set Acceleration or CharacterMovement cast success
  -> Set IsAccelerating(Acceleration > is_accelerating_threshold)
```

If `guard_pawn_owner=false`, the branch is skipped and the setter executes
after `TryGetPawnOwner`.

When Unreal materializes `TryGetPawnOwner`, `GetVelocity`, `GetActorRotation`,
`CalculateDirection`, `GetMovementComponent`, `IsFalling`, or
`GetCurrentAcceleration` as pure Blueprint nodes, the command keeps the same
data dependency and routes execution directly to the next impure node in the
setter chain.

`Speed` is the default variable name. The command accepts `speed_variable` and
creates a float variable when `create_variable_if_missing=true`.

`Direction` is optional behind `include_direction=true`. The command accepts
`direction_variable` and creates a float variable when
`create_direction_variable_if_missing=true`.

`IsInAir` is optional behind `include_is_in_air=true`. The command accepts
`is_in_air_variable` and creates a bool variable when
`create_is_in_air_variable_if_missing=true`.

`Acceleration` is optional behind `include_acceleration=true`. The command
accepts `acceleration_variable` and creates a float variable when
`create_acceleration_variable_if_missing=true`.

`IsAccelerating` is optional behind `include_is_accelerating=true`. The command
accepts `is_accelerating_variable`, creates a bool variable when
`create_is_accelerating_variable_if_missing=true`, and compares acceleration
magnitude against `is_accelerating_threshold` (default `3.0`).

Existing EventGraph links are preserved by default. Pass
`replace_existing_links=true` when deliberately rewriting an existing sample
target's conflicting pins.

## Response Contract

The response includes:

- `sample_only=true`
- `source_asset_modified=false`
- `original_assets_modified=false`
- target create/reuse flags
- `variables`, `nodes`, `created_nodes`, and `links`
- compile/save result and top-level success derived from requested compile/save
- `readback` from `inspect_blueprint_graph_call_topology`
- partial target fields on failures after target preparation

## Non-Goals

- Crouch, gait, aim offset, or turn-in-place variables.
- Arbitrary EventGraph rewrites.
- Editing production/original AnimBPs.
- ControlRig authoring; that is handled by a separate learning route.

## Planner Composition

Implemented follow-up: `bp_authoring_planner.py` and
`bp_authoring_job_contract.py` now expose an automatic sample locomotion
pipeline that runs this EventGraph driver first, then reuses the same
sample/temp target with `ensure_anim_state_machine_sample_variant`.

The default planner contract authors:

- `Speed`, `Direction`, `IsInAir`, `Acceleration`, and `IsAccelerating` from
  owning pawn data;
- `replace_existing_links=true` for the sample duplicate so a source AnimBP
  that already has locomotion EventGraph links can be normalized without
  touching the source asset;
- an Idle state backed by the default sample idle sequence;
- a Move state backed by the default sample 1D locomotion BlendSpace with
  BlendSpacePlayer `X -> Speed`;
- `Idle -> Move` and `Move -> Idle` bounded `float_compare` rules on `Speed`;
- readback through both `inspect_blueprint_graph_call_topology` and
  `inspect_anim_state_machine_transitions`.

Reusable bridge smoke:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\run_anim_bp_locomotion_pipeline_smoke.ps1
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_anim_bp_locomotion_pipeline_bridge.py --json
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\planner_driven_bp_authoring_smoke.py --request "Create an automatic sample Animation Blueprint locomotion pipeline with Speed EventGraph driving and a sample state machine." --run-live --require-live --no-write
```

## Follow-Up Candidates

- Optional gait/crouch flags from project-specific movement state.
- Turn-in-place and gait remain review-required project-specific locomotion
  state, not part of the generic sample pipeline.
